# Options always mean feedback HTML + a link

Whenever Grant asks for options, variants, directions, mockups, "give me 3 options", design choices, or similar review decisions:

1. **Always** build a standalone interactive feedback HTML page (Looks good / Needs work toggle, comment box per option, Copy feedback panel, light/dark toggle). On this repo, follow `.claude/skills/oscarfinch-feedback-html/SKILL.md` and its `template.html`. On other projects, use that same shape unless a project-specific feedback-HTML skill exists.
2. **Always** give him a working, clickable link he can open in a browser in the same reply. A repo path, PR URL, or screenshot alone is not enough.
3. For this GitHub repo, after pushing the HTML file, the default openable link is:
   `https://htmlpreview.github.io/?https://raw.githubusercontent.com/<owner>/<repo>/<branch>/<path-to-file>.html`
   Verify the raw file returns HTTP 200 before sending the link.
4. Do **not** wait for him to say "in HTML", "as an artifact", or "give me the link". Asking for options already means this format.
5. Prose can introduce the options, but the HTML link is mandatory in the same turn.
